Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: SDL3 as the window and its input, chosen at run time (PS2X_PLATFORM=sdl3)

The window, the keyboard, the mouse and the controllers through SDL3 instead of raylib's GLFW, with raylib staying the
default: PS2X_PLATFORM=sdl3 (environment or settings.ini; F5 > Display > Window system) in a build with PS2X_SDL3
(CMake option, off by default: nothing more is fetched or built). The Vulkan track's milestone 5 (the plan's P2), built
together with milestone 3 (Vulkan presenting the window) since a window without raylib needs its input.

The runtime and the game call raylib for the window, input and the overlays' 2D drawing about 440 times; none of
those calls change. In a build with PS2X_SDL3, raylib's own definitions of those calls (ps2_raylib_calls.h: the
window, the monitors, the cursor, keys, mouse, gamepads, the clock, BeginDrawing / EndDrawing, the 2D shapes, text,
fonts and textures) are compiled as rl_<name> - a forced include on raylib's rcore.c, rshapes.c, rtextures.c and
rtext.c - and ps2_platform.cpp defines the calls: raylib's own by default, SDL3's under PS2X_PLATFORM=sdl3. The
linker keeps the two lists in step (a name in one and not the other is defined twice or not at all).

Under SDL3:
- The window is SDL's, made and pumped on the main thread; raylib's input semantics kept (pressed against the last
  poll, the queues emptied each poll, the wheel per poll, the exit key, a minimised window's loop waiting).
- Keys by place (SDL scancodes as raylib's key codes, which name places too); the mouse, relative while captured.
- Gamepads are SDL_Gamepad (SDL's controller database, Steam Input's virtual pads), read as raylib's (the same buttons
  by place, triggers as GLFW's -1..1 and as buttons past a tenth). The game's vibration goes to SDL_RumbleGamepad on
  the pad the game reads (ps2_xinput_rumble.cpp: under SDL3 its motors are SDL's, renewed while they run); the light
  bar from PS2X_SONYPAD_LIGHTBAR; ps2_platform::gamepadType / gamepadTriggerRumble / gamepadLed for a game's own use.
  The native DualSense / DualShock 4 code keeps Sony pads' HID unless PS2X_GAMEPAD_BACKEND=glfw (SDL is then told to
  leave their HID alone, so the two never both write their output reports).
- No OpenGL: each window picture is one ImGui frame from BeginDrawing to EndDrawing - the picture (DrawTexturePro) and
  the 2D overlays (text, rectangles, circles, triangles, lines, scissors; raylib's default font is ImGui's default
  font, a font from LoadFontEx is ImGui's from the same file) in its background draw list, the ImGui panels over them.
  The overlay host (patch 0175) is SDL3's: imgui_impl_sdl3 feeds ImGui every event, so the game's rlImGui input
  workarounds stay off.
- A presenter draws the frame: SDL's renderer by default (it picks Direct3D 11 / 12, Vulkan, Metal or OpenGL; its
  VSync follows the VSync setting), or one a graphics backend sets before the window is made (ps2_platform::
  setPresenter: Vulkan presenting the window itself). Textures are the presenter's.
- The GS's GPU renderer (OpenGL) does not start, nor does the DXGI present (GL interop): the GS's software picture
  shows what the native renderer does not draw. A native renderer's picture reaches the window as CPU pixels.
- LoadImageFromScreen gives the last picture presented (PS2X_SHOT_KEEP=1 keeps each one from the start; otherwise
  from the first request on) - the test shots work in a hidden window.
- ps2_platform::windowScreenHz(): the refresh rate of the window's screen from SDL's display mode, for pacing where
  the system gives no vertical blank timing (a Linux host: the linux-port fork's monitor-refresh cap, from the window).

Not changed: a build without PS2X_SDL3 (ps2_platform.cpp then only answers "raylib"), and PS2X_PLATFORM unset in a
build with it (every call raylib's own).

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/CMakeLists.txt b/ps2xRuntime/CMakeLists.txt
index c35858e..7ce09b0 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -149,6 +149,47 @@ else()
         target_link_libraries(rlImGui PUBLIC raylib imgui)
     endif()
 
+    # (The Vulkan track's milestone 3) SDL3 as the window and its input, chosen at run time: PS2X_PLATFORM=sdl3
+    # (ps2_platform.h). Off by default: nothing more is fetched or built. With it, raylib's window, input and 2D calls
+    # are compiled into raylib as rl_<name> (ps2_raylib_calls.h, a forced include on raylib's own sources) and the
+    # runtime answers them (ps2_platform.cpp): raylib's own by default, SDL3's under PS2X_PLATFORM=sdl3.
+    option(PS2X_SDL3 "SDL3 as the window and its input at run time (PS2X_PLATFORM=sdl3)" OFF)
+    if(PS2X_SDL3)
+        if(NOT PS2X_ENABLE_DEBUG_UI OR PS2X_IS_ANDROID)
+            message(FATAL_ERROR "PS2X_SDL3 draws its overlays with the debug UI's ImGui: it needs PS2X_ENABLE_DEBUG_UI")
+        endif()
+        if(NOT TARGET SDL3::SDL3-static)
+            set(SDL_SHARED OFF)
+            set(SDL_STATIC ON)
+            set(SDL_TEST_LIBRARY OFF)
+            set(SDL_TESTS OFF)
+            set(SDL_EXAMPLES OFF)
+            set(SDL_INSTALL OFF)
+            FetchContent_Declare(ps2x_sdl3
+                GIT_REPOSITORY https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL.git
+                GIT_TAG release-3.4.18
+                GIT_SHALLOW TRUE)
+            FetchContent_MakeAvailable(ps2x_sdl3)
+        endif()
+        add_library(ps2x_imgui_sdl3 STATIC
+            "${PS2X_IMGUI_SOURCE_DIR}/backends/imgui_impl_sdl3.cpp"
+            "${PS2X_IMGUI_SOURCE_DIR}/backends/imgui_impl_sdlrenderer3.cpp")
+        target_include_directories(ps2x_imgui_sdl3 PUBLIC "${PS2X_IMGUI_SOURCE_DIR}")
+        target_link_libraries(ps2x_imgui_sdl3 PUBLIC imgui SDL3::SDL3-static)
+        set(_ps2x_raylib_calls "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/lib/ps2_raylib_calls.h")
+        foreach(_ps2x_rl rcore.c rshapes.c rtextures.c rtext.c)
+            set_property(SOURCE "${raylib_SOURCE_DIR}/src/${_ps2x_rl}" DIRECTORY "${raylib_SOURCE_DIR}/src"
+                APPEND PROPERTY COMPILE_DEFINITIONS PS2X_RAYLIB_RENAME=1)
+            if(MSVC)
+                set_property(SOURCE "${raylib_SOURCE_DIR}/src/${_ps2x_rl}" DIRECTORY "${raylib_SOURCE_DIR}/src"
+                    APPEND PROPERTY COMPILE_OPTIONS "/FI${_ps2x_raylib_calls}")
+            else()
+                set_property(SOURCE "${raylib_SOURCE_DIR}/src/${_ps2x_rl}" DIRECTORY "${raylib_SOURCE_DIR}/src"
+                    APPEND PROPERTY COMPILE_OPTIONS "-include" "${_ps2x_raylib_calls}")
+            endif()
+        endforeach()
+    endif()
+
     # xbyak (header-only x86-64 assembler) for the VU1 JIT.
     if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "^(AMD64|x86_64|amd64)$" AND NOT PS2X_IS_ANDROID)
         FetchContent_Declare(
@@ -447,6 +488,7 @@ add_library(ps2_runtime STATIC
     src/lib/ps2_iop_host.cpp
     src/lib/ps2_memory.cpp
     src/lib/ps2_pad.cpp
+    src/lib/ps2_platform.cpp
     src/lib/ps2_sony_pad.cpp
     src/lib/ps2_sony_pad_host.cpp
     src/lib/ps2_xinput_rumble.cpp
@@ -498,6 +540,11 @@ endif()
 target_compile_definitions(ps2_runtime PRIVATE
     PS2X_HAS_FFMPEG=$<BOOL:${PS2X_ENABLE_FFMPEG}>
 )
+if(PS2X_SDL3)
+    # (only ps2_platform.cpp knows SDL3: the rest of the runtime keeps its command lines)
+    set_source_files_properties(src/lib/ps2_platform.cpp PROPERTIES COMPILE_DEFINITIONS PS2X_HAS_SDL3=1)
+    target_link_libraries(ps2_runtime PRIVATE ps2x_imgui_sdl3 SDL3::SDL3-static imgui)
+endif()
 
 file(GLOB_RECURSE KERNEL_SRC_FILES CONFIGURE_DEPENDS
     "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/lib/Kernel/*.cpp"
diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_platform.h b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_platform.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0e89e03
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_platform.h
@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+#pragma once
+
+// The window and its input: raylib's (GLFW, the default) or SDL3's (PS2X_PLATFORM=sdl3, in a build with PS2X_SDL3).
+//
+// The runtime and a game call raylib for the window, the keyboard, the mouse, the gamepads and the overlays' 2D drawing,
+// as before. In a build with SDL3 the runtime answers those calls itself (ps2_platform.cpp; the list is
+// ps2_raylib_calls.h): raylib's own definitions are compiled as rl_<name>, and each call goes to raylib's or, under
+// PS2X_PLATFORM=sdl3, to SDL3's window and input and to the overlays' ImGui drawing. With PS2X_PLATFORM unset (or
+// raylib) every call is raylib's own; a build without PS2X_SDL3 has none of this. raylib's other calls (images, files,
+// audio) are raylib's under both.
+//
+// Under SDL3 there is no OpenGL. Each window picture is one ImGui frame from BeginDrawing to EndDrawing: the picture
+// (DrawTexturePro) and the 2D overlays (DrawText, the rectangles...) go into its background draw list, the ImGui panels
+// over them (the overlay host is SDL3's: ps2_overlay.h). A presenter draws the frame into the window: SDL's 2D renderer
+// by default (it picks Direct3D 11 or 12, Vulkan, Metal or OpenGL for the system), or one a graphics backend sets
+// (setPresenter: the native renderer's Vulkan backend presents into the window's own swapchain). The GS's GPU renderer
+// (OpenGL) does not start; the GS's software picture shows what the native renderer does not draw.
+//
+// Controllers: SDL's gamepads (its controller database; Steam Input's virtual pads; Xbox, PlayStation, Switch and
+// others), read as raylib's gamepads (the same buttons and axes). The game's vibration goes to SDL_RumbleGamepad. A
+// Sony pad that the native DualSense / DualShock 4 code (ps2_sony_pad.h) takes stays its own: SDL then leaves Sony pads'
+// HID to it (PS2X_GAMEPAD_BACKEND auto or sony); with glfw (Steam Input, DS4Windows) SDL takes them too, its light bar
+// from PS2X_SONYPAD_LIGHTBAR.
+//
+//   PS2X_PLATFORM=raylib | sdl3   read once, when the window is made (settings.ini too)
+//   PS2X_SDL_LOG=1                the window's and the gamepads' events in the log
+#include <cstdint>
+
+namespace ps2_platform
+{
+    bool sdl3();         // the window is SDL3's (PS2X_PLATFORM=sdl3 in a build with it)
+    const char *name();  // "raylib" or "sdl3"
+    void *sdlWindow();   // the SDL_Window, under SDL3 (else null)
+    // The settings panel's choice of the two (F5 > Display, a restart): in a build with SDL3 only.
+    void addSetting();
+
+    // ---- under SDL3: what draws the window's pictures ----------------------------------------------------------
+    // Textures (LoadTextureFromImage's, a backend's own pictures) are the presenter's: ImGui draws them by its
+    // ImTextureID. Every call on the window's thread (the main thread).
+    struct Presenter
+    {
+        const char *name = "";
+        // Before the window is made: the SDL window flags it needs (SDL_WINDOW_VULKAN...).
+        uint64_t windowFlags = 0u;
+        // The window exists: set up (ImGui's renderer backend too). False: this presenter cannot draw here.
+        bool (*open)(void *sdlWindow) = nullptr;
+        void (*close)() = nullptr;
+        // Before ImGui's frame of a picture (the renderer backend's NewFrame): false when it cannot draw one now (its
+        // device not made yet, the window hidden...) - that picture is then left out.
+        bool (*newFrame)() = nullptr;
+        // The picture's ImGui draw data (ImDrawData*) drawn over black, and presented.
+        void (*present)(void *imDrawData) = nullptr;
+        // Textures, RGBA8: made (`linear`: bilinear filtering, else nearest), their pixels replaced (rows of
+        // `pitch` bytes), let go. A texture 0 is none.
+        uint64_t (*makeTexture)(int width, int height, bool linear) = nullptr;
+        void (*updateTexture)(uint64_t texture, const void *pixels, int pitch) = nullptr;
+        void (*setTextureFilter)(uint64_t texture, bool linear) = nullptr;
+        void (*dropTexture)(uint64_t texture) = nullptr;
+        // A texture as ImGui's ImTextureID, when it is drawn (null: the same value). 0: not drawable now.
+        uint64_t (*imguiTexture)(uint64_t texture) = nullptr;
+        // The last picture presented, as RGBA8 rows (LoadImageFromScreen: a test's or the player's shot). Optional.
+        bool (*readLastPicture)(void *rgba, int width, int height) = nullptr;
+    };
+    // Before the window is made (a graphics backend that presents itself). The default: SDL's 2D renderer.
+    void setPresenter(const Presenter &presenter);
+    const char *presenterName();
+    // A texture of the presenter's own (a backend's picture) as a raylib texture id, for the window's loop to draw
+    // with DrawTexturePro; updateExternalTexture when it is another one or another size. 0: none.
+    unsigned int registerExternalTexture(uint64_t texture, int width, int height);
+    void updateExternalTexture(unsigned int id, uint64_t texture, int width, int height);
+    void dropExternalTexture(unsigned int id);
+
+    // ---- under SDL3: the controllers -----------------------------------------------------------------------
+    // The game's vibration on the gamepad it reads (raylib's gamepad index, -1: the first one): low and high frequency
+    // motors, 0..65535.
+    // False when there is no such SDL gamepad (raylib's platform: XInput does it, ps2_xinput_rumble.cpp).
+    bool gamepadRumble(int gamepad, uint16_t low, uint16_t high);
+    // The trigger motors (Xbox One and later; SDL_RumbleGamepadTriggers), 0..65535: false where there are none.
+    bool gamepadTriggerRumble(int gamepad, uint16_t left, uint16_t right);
+    // The light bar or LED (DualSense, DualShock 4, Switch's home light...): false where there is none.
+    bool gamepadLed(int gamepad, uint8_t red, uint8_t green, uint8_t blue);
+    // SDL's kind of pad: "xbox360", "xboxone", "ps3", "ps4", "ps5", "switchpro", "joyconpair", "gamecube", "steam"...,
+    // or "" (raylib's platform, or no such gamepad).
+    const char *gamepadType(int gamepad);
+
+    // ---- the screen's refresh (kayliox's Linux note: there may be no vertical blank timing) ---------------------
+    // The refresh rate of the screen the window is on (SDL's display mode), 0 when not known.
+    float windowScreenHz();
+}
